{
  "category": "Iron Snake Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "Its body has been compressed deep under the ground. As a result, it is even harder than a diamond.",
      "version": "gold"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is said that if an ONIX lives for over 100 years, its composition changes to become diamond-like.",
      "version": "silver"
    },
    {
      "text": "The many small metal particles that cover this POKéMON's body reflect bright light well.",
      "version": "crystal"
    },
    {
      "text": "STEELIX lives even further underground than ONIX. This POKéMON is known to dig towards the earth’s core. There are records of this POKéMON reaching a depth of over six-tenths of a mile underground.",
      "version": "ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "STEELIX lives even further underground than ONIX. This POKéMON is known to dig towards the earth’s core. There are records of this POKéMON reaching a depth of over six-tenths of a mile underground.",
      "version": "sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "STEELIX live even further underground than ONIX. This POKéMON is known to dig toward the earth’s core, reaching a depth of over six-tenths of a mile underground.",
      "version": "emerald"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is said that if an ONIX lives for over 100 years, its composition changes to become diamond-like.",
      "version": "firered"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its body has been compressed deep under the ground. As a result, it is even harder than diamond.",
      "version": "leafgreen"
    },
    {
      "text": "Tempered underground under high pressure and heat, its body is harder than any metal.",
      "version": "diamond"
    },
    {
      "text": "It chews its way through boulders with its sturdy jaws. Its eyes can see in the darkness underground.",
      "version": "pearl"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is thought its body transformed as a result of iron accumulating internally from swallowing soil.",
      "version": "platinum"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its body has been compressed deep under the ground. As a result, it is even harder than a diamond.",
